d517a13e0b31bb29433b67715f29f26120315d51.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 2:27PM MDT until August 15 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Adams County in northeastern Colorado...\nWestern Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nSoutheastern Denver County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 430 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Water over roadways. Ponding of water in urban or other\nareas is occurring or is imminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 226 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. This may cause urban and small stream flooding. Up\nto 0.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDenver, Aurora, eastern Centennial, Englewood, Greenwood Village,\nSheridan, Buckley SFB, Arapahoe Park, Cherry Hills Village,\nFoxfield and Cherry Creek Reservoir.","ends":"2026-08-15T16:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1f99c4123bab47c11a356083c849ccd983e7854.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1f99c4123bab47c11a356083c849ccd983e7854.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151912 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 112 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Another round of showers and thunderstorms this afternoon and evening. Heavy rainfall and flash flooding are the main threats today. A few thunderstorms could become severe, with strong winds and hail possible. - Monsoon moisture lasts through Sunday, brin","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format